/-!
# The completion functor of a finite family of global sections

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪`. Writing `Č(f)`
for the extended alternating Čech complex

`𝒪 → ∏_{i₀} 𝒪_{f_{i₀}} → ∏_{i₀ < i₁} 𝒪_{f_{i₀} f_{i₁}} → ⋯ → 𝒪_{f_1 ⋯ f_r}`,

the candidate completion functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is `K ↦ K^∧ := R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)`,
and the map `K ⟶ K^∧` is derived internal Hom into `K` applied to the augmentation
`Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪`, followed by the identification `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K) = K`. This file constructs that
functor, that augmentation and that map, and records what their universal property still needs.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.cechAugmentation`: the augmentation `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]`, the
  identification of the degree-zero term `𝒪_{f_∅}` of the Čech complex with `𝒪` read as a map
  of complexes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor`: the completion functor
  `K ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` on `D(𝒪)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit`: the natural transformation
  `𝟭 ⟶ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), -)` induced by the augmentation, that is the map `K ⟶ K^∧`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_extendedAlternatingCech_X_of_neg` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_extendedAlternatingCech_X_of_lt`: the Čech complex
  vanishes outside the degrees `0, …, r`. Vanishing in negative degrees is what makes the
  augmentation a map of complexes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionUnit_app`: the map `K ⟶ K^∧` read as the composite of
  the identification `K = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, K)` with the map induced by the augmentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE_extendedAlternatingCech`:
  the dévissage of `Č(f)^{≥ 1}` along its stupid filtration, giving
  `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)^{≥ 1}, K) = 0` from the vanishing at the non-empty subproducts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal` of
  `CompletionUnitIso.lean`: `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible as soon as `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_S}, K) = 0` for
  every non-empty `S`; it and the stupid-filtration identities it uses —
  `ιStupidTrunc_comp_cechAugmentation`, `isIso_ιStupidTrunc_extendedAlternatingCech`,
  `isIso_cechAugmentationZero` and the boundedness `finite_support_extendedAlternatingCech` —
  are proved there, above this module, and not repeated here. Raising the
  hypothesis to the generators `f_i` alone is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_memVanishingIdeal_generators` of
  `CompletionUnitInvertible.lean`, which is a separate module only because the implication
  (1) ⇒ (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0997] it uses lives above this one; the `hη` hypothesis below is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete` of that same
  module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion`:
  [Stacks, Tag 099F] for the ideal sheaf generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, reduced to the three
  remaining properties of this completion functor — that every `K^∧` is derived complete, that
  `K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible on derived-complete objects, and that the completion functor carries
  `K ⟶ K^∧` to `K^∧ ⟶ (K^∧)^∧`. All three are now proved; see the note below. The version
  taking only the third, at the ideal sheaf `ℐ` generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_comm`
  of `GeneratedIdealComplete.lean`, and the version taking nothing at all is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` of
  `GeneratedIdealAdjoint.lean`.

## Implementation notes

The universes are those of [Stacks, Tag 0996], a `RingedSite.{u, u, u}` with coefficient
universe `u`, and not the three independent universes of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete`. The restriction is inherited, not chosen:
the derived internal Hom bifunctor
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHomBifunctor` and the localization comparison
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHom_restrictScalarsIso` of
`HomAfterLocalization.lean` — which is [Stacks, Tag 0996], the third step of the source's
proof — are both stated only there, an iterated internal Hom forcing the site universes and the
module universe together. The derived category is the standard model, as it is everywhere in
this directory.

The augmentation goes *out of* the Čech complex: derived internal Hom is contravariant in its
source, so the map `K ⟶ K^∧` comes from a map `Č(f) ⟶ 𝒪[0]`, not from the map `𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪_{f_∅}`
into the degree-zero term. That map of complexes is the inverse of the identification of the
degree-zero term with `𝒪` — the degree-zero term is a product over the subsets of cardinality
zero, of which `∅` is the only one, and `𝒪_{f_∅} = 𝒪_1` is `𝒪` — and is a map of complexes
because the Čech complex vanishes in degree `-1`, its index type there being empty.

### Tags 099B and 099F

The `@[stacks 099B]` attribute is not attached here because this file builds `(Φ, η)` and does
not prove its universal property. That property is now proved, in `GeneratedIdealAdjoint.lean`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.bijective_precomp_completionUnit_generatedIdealSheaf` is the
displayed assertion of the tag and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` is its
conclusion, both at the tag's own ideal sheaf and with nothing carried. The tag's other
registrant is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_forall_isNilpotent` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletionRinged/NilpotentIdeal.lean`,
which proves the conclusion under the restriction that the local sections of `ℐ` be nilpotent,
where the left adjoint is the identity. The three constituents of the universal property are
reduced to named statements by `isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion` below, and the
note on each of them records where it is proved.

Note first what the reduction leaves free: the ideal sheaf `I`. The tag's `ℐ` is the one
*generated by* `f_1, …, f_r`, and that sheaf of ideals is now constructed —
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf` of `GeneratedIdealSheaf.lean` — so the tag can
be stated at its own hypothesis, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completion_generatedIdealSheaf`
there.

1. **Derived completeness of `K^∧` (`hΦ`) — proved.** It is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_completionFunctor_obj` of
   `GeneratedIdealComplete.lean`, at the ideal sheaf `ℐ` generated by `f_1, …, f_r` and with
   nothing carried. The ingredients are as follows.

   *The iterated internal Hom* — available. The first step is the derived tensor–Hom adjunction
   `R𝑆heafHom(A, R𝑆heafHom(B, K)) ≅ R𝑆heafHom(A ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 B, K)`, and that is
   [Stacks, Tag 08J9], `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCurryIso` of
   `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/InternalHom/DerivedCurrying.lean`, for
   arbitrary objects of `D(𝒪)` and with three-variable naturality in
   `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/InternalHom/DerivedCurryingNaturality.lean`. Read at `B = Č(f)` it is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHom_completionFunctor_iso` of
   `CompletionCurry.lean`, `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A, K^∧) = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 Č(f), K)`, with the
   consequence the completeness criterion consumes —
   `isZero_derivedSheafHom_completionFunctor_of_isZero_derivedTensor` — beside it. No
   K-flatness of `Č(f)` enters: Tag 08J9 chooses a K-flat model of its middle variable itself.
   The source instead uses [Stacks, Tag 0996] (3); parts (1), (2) and (3) of that tag are all
   proved too, respectively as
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHom_awayRestrictScalarsIso` of
   `LocalizationAtGlobalSection.lean`,
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHom_coextendScalarsIso` of
   `HomIntoCoextension.lean` and
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedSheafHom_awayMulCurryIso` of
   `AwayInternalHomMulDerived.lean`, but they identify the Hom when *both* arguments are
   localizations of the structure sheaf, which is not the shape the first step needs.

   The interchange isomorphism
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedTensorHomInterchange_of_isFiniteFreeSummand` of
   `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/InternalHom/DerivedTensorHomInterchangeStrictlyPerfect.lean` remains *unrelated* to all of this: it
   inverts [Stacks, Tag 0BYU]'s comparison `K ⊗^𝐋 R𝑆heafHom(C, L) ⟶ R𝑆heafHom(C, K ⊗^𝐋 L)`,
   whose tensor factor is in the target.

   *Base change of the Čech complex* — available, and with no side condition at a generator:
   `RingedSite.isZero_derivedTensor_awayComplex_extendedAlternatingCech_prodGlobalSection`
   of `CechBaseChange.lean` is `𝒪_{f_V} ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 Č(f) = 0` for every `V` containing some index.
   The complex-level identification this note called "nowhere" was not what was needed: what the
   contractibility of `𝒪_g ⊗_𝒪 Č(f)` really asks is that tensoring with `𝒪_g` invert the
   transition maps of the Čech system, which is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_awayTensorFunctor_map_awayModuleTransition` there, proved
   from the naturality of `𝒪_g ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_h ≅ 𝒪_{gh}` in `h`
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.awayTensorSheafIso_naturality_right` of
   `AwayTensorNaturality.lean`).

   *Slice sites* — not needed. The argument does not use that the restriction of
   `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` to a slice is the Čech completion there: the vanishing at the generators is proved on the site itself and is
   carried to the slices by the restriction stability of the vanishing locus of
   [Stacks, Tag 0998].

   *Local generation* — proved. A local section of `ℐ` over `U` is only *locally* an
   `𝒪`-combination of `f_1, …, f_r`
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mem_generatedIdealSheaf_iff`), so the generators suffice only
   together with all four clauses of [Stacks, Tag 0998]: multiplicativity, additivity,
   restriction stability and the sheaf condition. All four are proved — see the note of
   `VanishingIdeal.lean` — the last of them, which the source omits, being
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_of_coversTop` of `VanishingIdealLocal.lean`.
   Assembling them is
   `RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal`,
   which is stated for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)` and not only for a completion.

2. **Invertibility of `K ⟶ K^∧` on a derived-complete `K` (`hη`).** The source deduces it from
   the vanishing of `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_{f_S}, K)` for every non-empty `S`, which is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.MemVanishingIdeal` of `VanishingIdeal.lean`.

   *Getting the vanishing.* [Stacks, Tag 0997] is proved, so the only step left on this side
   is the descent to the site. (1) ⇔ (3) is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_derivedAwayModule_iff_isDerivedCompleteAt`
   of `VanishingCriterionTelescope.lean`, so `T(K, g) = 0` gives `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_g, K) = 0` for a
   global section `g`; and the multiplicativity from `f_i` to `f_S` for `S ∋ i` is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_of_mem` of
   `CompletionUnitInvertible.lean`, which is
   (1) ⇒ (2) of that tag —
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_awayRestrictScalars_of_isZero` of
   `VanishingCriterionCoextension.lean` — followed by the propagation
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_of_subset`.

   **The descent is proved, and with it `hη`.** `IsDerivedComplete X I K` is the condition over
   every object `U` of the site about `K|_U`, so it gives `T(K|_U, g) = 0` for every local
   section `g` of `I` over `U` and not `T(K, f_i) = 0` on the site itself; descending the latter
   from the former is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedCompleteAt_of_forall_isDerivedCompleteAt_over` of
   `SliceRestrictionDescent.lean`, whose two inputs — the slice restrictions jointly reflect
   isomorphisms in `D(𝒪)`, and each commutes with the countable product that
   `IsDerivedCompleteAt` quantifies over — are proved there.

   `hη` itself is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete` of
   `CompletionUnitInvertible.lean`, whose only hypothesis beyond derived completeness is the
   membership of the generators in `I` — this reduction leaves `I` free, and
   `IsDerivedComplete X I K` says nothing about `f_i` unless `f_i` is a section of `I`. At the
   ideal sheaf `ℐ` generated by the `f_i`, where `GeneratedIdealSheaf.lean` discharges that
   membership, it becomes
   `RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`,
   which carries nothing at all. The reduction with `hη` discharged and `hΦ`, `hcomm` still
   hypotheses is
   `isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isDerivedComplete_completion`.

   *Using it* — done. The argument is the stupid filtration of the bounded complex `Č(f)`: the
   augmentation is a degreewise split epimorphism with kernel the truncation `Č(f)^{≥ 1}`, whose
   terms are finite products of the sheaves `𝒪_{f_S}` with `S` non-empty, so
   `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)^{≥ 1}, K) = 0` by induction on the finitely many non-zero terms. That is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE_extendedAlternatingCech`
   below, and the invertibility it gives is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_forall_memVanishingIdeal` of
   `CompletionUnitIso.lean`. The
   induction is
   `Stacks.DerivedCategory.BoundedInduction.property_of_bounded_complex_stupidTruncGE` of
   `StacksFrontier/Algebra/Homology/DerivedCategory/StupidTruncationTriangle.lean`, whose extension
   hypothesis is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_obj₂_of_distTriang` and
   whose boundedness hypothesis is `finite_support_extendedAlternatingCech` of
   `CompletionUnitIso.lean`, reproved inline below. Its three
   further inputs are all available now.

   *Finite products.* The `p`-th term of `Č(f)` is a product over
   `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.Idx r p`, a finite type, and the binary
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_biprod` was the only form. The
   `Fintype`-indexed one is now
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_single_pi` of
   `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/InternalHom/DerivedHomCoproducts.lean`, which
   takes the product in the abelian category and needs no preservation of it by the single
   functor: an additive functor annihilates a finite biproduct whose factors it annihilates,
   because the identity of a finite biproduct is the finite sum `∑ j, π j ≫ ι j`. The countable
   coproduct form `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pi_lift_derivedSheafHom_sigma` of the same
   file is a different statement and is not used here.

   *Shift in the contravariant variable* — available. The induction's hypothesis is about the
   `p`-th term placed *in degree `p`*, so one needs `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A⟦n⟧, K) = 0` from
   `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A, K) = 0`. That is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_shift_iff` of `VanishingIdeal.lean`, read
   at the single functors by `isZero_derivedSheafHom_single_iff_single_zero` below. It needs no
   `CategoryTheory.Functor.CommShift` for the derived internal Hom, of which there is none in
   either variable: the triangle `A ⟶ 0 ⟶ A⟦1⟧` with identity third morphism is distinguished
   because its middle vertex is zero, and
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_distinguished_derivedSheafHom` carries it to a
   distinguished triangle whose outer vertices are `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A⟦1⟧, K)` and
   `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A, K)` and whose middle vertex is zero.

   *The unit* — available. `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ιStupidTrunc_comp_cechAugmentation`
   of `CompletionUnitIso.lean` identifies `cechAugmentation` with the second morphism of the
   `p = 0` stupid-truncation triangle, under `Č(f)^{≥ 0} ≅ Č(f)`
   (`isIso_ιStupidTrunc_extendedAlternatingCech`, the Čech complex vanishing in negative degrees)
   and `(Č(f).X 0)[0] ≅ 𝒪[0]` (`isIso_cechAugmentationZero`, the degree-zero term being a
   product over a type with a unique element).

3. **The third hypothesis**, `Φ η_K = η_{Φ K}`, of
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_completionFunctor`
   — **proved.** It is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor_map_completionUnit_app` of
   `GeneratedIdealAdjoint.lean`, and with it [Stacks, Tag 099F] at the ideal sheaf `ℐ` generated
   by `f_1, …, f_r` is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` there,
   with nothing carried.

   It does **not** follow from 1 and 2: the two-object counterexample
   `CompletionUnitSharpness.exists_completionFunctor_and_not_isRightAdjoint_ι`
   of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletion.lean` is a `(Φ, η)`
   satisfying both whose inclusion has no left adjoint, so no argument from 1 and 2 alone can
   reach it. What it is a sufficient condition for is the invertibility of `Φ η_K`, the
   hypothesis of `Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_of_completionFunctor`, and that is what
   is proved first: by the stupid-filtration triangle of 2 the cone of `η_K` is
   `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)^{≥ 1}, K)`, so `Φ η_K` is invertible as soon as
   `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f)^{≥ 1}, K)) = 0`, and that is
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_completionFunctor_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE`. Its
   input is the identification
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctorDerivedSheafHomIso`,
   `(R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A, K))^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(A, K^∧)`, which is the iterated internal Hom of
   [Stacks, Tag 08J9] in `CompletionCurry.lean` applied twice with the two tensor factors
   exchanged by the commutativity constraint of [Stacks, Tag 0FPT]; read at
   `A = Č(f)^{≥ 1}` it turns the vanishing into the dévissage of 2 applied to `K^∧`, whose own
   hypothesis is the vanishing at the generators that 1 already proves. So no new vanishing and
   no new base change is needed, and the contractibility of `Č(f) ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_{f_S}` enters only
   through 1.

   The equality is then deduced from the invertibility: with 1, 2 and the invertibility in hand,
   precomposition with `η_K` is injective on morphisms into a derived-complete object
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.bijective_precomp_completionUnit_generatedIdealSheaf`, which is
   the displayed assertion of [Stacks, Tag 099B]), and naturality of `η` at `η_K` says that
   `Φ η_K` and `η_{Φ K}` agree after that precomposition.

